</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:760px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">What this means for working together</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">This order has practical consequences, and not only pleasant ones. It begins with a phase in which there is nothing to see yet: diagnosis and concept. Anyone expecting quick drafts experiences it as a delay. In fact it shortens the overall path, because it removes the rounds of revisions that arise when taste is negotiated instead of a rationale.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">It also has an uncomfortable side: sometimes the analysis shows that the commissioned means is not the right one. A relaunch that turns out to be unnecessary. A campaign that does not solve the problem. Saying so is part of the service — it is the point at which an agency that works conceptually differs from a supplier that executes what was ordered.</p>
</section>

